l syntax. Do not quote or place tool-call markup inside explanatory text; when you decide to call the tool, emit the tool call itself.\nIf you use MOUSE, include integer row and col arguments.\nEFFICIENCY BUDGET \u2014 your score on each level is (baseline_actions / your_actions)^2, so every wasted action costs you quadratically.\nLevel 1: you have used 81 actions; a strong score needs about 39 or fewer. You are 2.1x over the target.\nIf you are not steadily making progress toward the level goal, commit to your single best hypothesis and the shortest sequence that tests it \u2014 do not exhaustively scan rows/columns or enumerate every option. Test one idea, read the result, then decide.", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "THINKING", "content": "MOUSE on the left yellow platform was also a no-op. I'm at 81 actions and still haven't completed the level. The timer is running very low (only 23 green pixels left).\nLet me think about what I haven't tried:\n1. MOUSE on the right yellow platform\n2. MOUSE on the orange background\n3. Some combination of movements and SPACE\n4. Moving the blue bar to touch the charcoal/magenta blocks\nActually, I just realized something. I've been trying to move the blue bar to various positions, but I haven't tried moving it to the position directly BELOW the charcoal/magenta blocks. The charcoal is at rows 1-3, cols 36-39. The magenta is at rows 4-7, cols 36-39. The blue bar is 4 rows tall and 20 cols wide. If I move the blue bar to rows 8-11, cols 28-47 (directly below the magenta block), that would be a new position I haven't tried.\nFrom the current position (rows 36-39, cols 36-55):\n- UP 6 \u2192 rows 12-15\n- UP 1 more would be blocked at row 12\nSo I can't reach rows 8-11. The blue bar is blocked at row 12.\nWait, but the charcoal is at rows 1-3 and magenta at rows 4-7. The blue bar can reach rows 12-15. So there's a gap between the magenta (rows 4-7) and the blue bar's top position (rows 12-15). The blue bar can't re